        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4624bafe-a1fa-59ea-bef1-c0606e787d79",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Kirby, Benny Goodman, O'Neill Spencer\n- Groups: John Kirby Sextet\n- Songs: \"Loch Lomond\", \"Undecided\", \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\"\n- Topics: chamber jazz, Scottish musical traditions\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1930s and early 1940s, John Kirby led a successful chamber jazz sextet.\n- John Kirby is also known for sideman work, especially with Benny Goodman.\n- John Kirby's sextet recorded hit songs including \"Loch Lomond\" and the debut recording of \"Undecided,\" which became a jazz standard.\n- O'Neill Spencer is best known for his work in the John Kirby Sextet.\n- In Scotland, \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\" is often played as the final piece of music during an evening of revelry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
